<div class="topos-title topos-mt1" data-title-type="mt1" data-style="mt1">The Book of Psalms</div><span class="topos-chapter" data-osis-id="PSA 1" data-n="1"></span><span class="topos-l" data-style="q1"><span class="topos-verse" data-osis-id="PSA 1:1" data-n="1"></span> <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H835" data-style="w">Blessed</span> <span class="topos-added" data-style="add">is</span> the <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H376" data-style="w">man</span> that <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H1980" data-style="w">walketh</span> not in the <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H6098" data-style="w">counsel</span> of the <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H7563" data-style="w">ungodly</span>, nor <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H5975" data-style="w">standeth</span> in the <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H1870" data-style="w">way</span> of <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H2400" data-style="w">sinners</span>, nor <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H3427" data-style="w">sitteth</span> in the <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H4186" data-style="w">seat</span> of the <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H3887" data-style="w">scornful</span>.<span class="topos-note topos-footnote" data-note-type="footnote" data-n="+" data-style="f"><span class="topos-char" data-style="fr">1.1 </span><span class="topos-char" data-style="ft">ungodly: or, wicked</span></span></span><br class="topos-l"><span class="topos-l" data-style="q1"><span class="topos-verse" data-osis-id="PSA 1:2" data-n="2"></span> But his <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H2656" data-style="w">delight</span> <span class="topos-added" data-style="add">is</span> in the <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H8451" data-style="w">law</span> of the <span class="topos-divine-name" data-style="nd"><span class="topos-w" data-strong="H3068" data-style="w">LORD</span></span>; and in his <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H8451" data-style="w">law</span> doth he <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H1897" data-style="w">meditate</span> <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H3119" data-style="w">day</span> and <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H3915" data-style="w">night</span>.</span><br class="topos-l"><span class="topos-l" data-style="q1"><span class="topos-verse" data-osis-id="PSA 1:3" data-n="3"></span> And he shall be like a <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H6086" data-style="w">tree</span> <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H8362" data-style="w">planted</span> by the <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H6388" data-style="w">rivers</span> of <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H4325" data-style="w">water</span>, that bringeth <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H5414" data-style="w">forth</span> his <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H6529" data-style="w">fruit</span> in his <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H6256" data-style="w">season</span>; his <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H5929" data-style="w">leaf</span> also shall not <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H5034" data-style="w">wither</span>; and whatsoever he <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H6213" data-style="w">doeth</span> shall <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H6743" data-style="w">prosper</span>.<span class="topos-note topos-footnote" data-note-type="footnote" data-n="+" data-style="f"><span class="topos-char" data-style="fr">1.3 </span><span class="topos-char" data-style="ft">wither: Heb. fade</span></span></span><br class="topos-l"><br class="topos-lb" data-style="b"><span class="topos-l" data-style="q1"><span class="topos-verse" data-osis-id="PSA 1:4" data-n="4"></span> The <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H7563" data-style="w">ungodly</span> <span class="topos-added" data-style="add">are</span> not so: but <span class="topos-added" data-style="add">are</span> like the <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H4671" data-style="w">chaff</span> which the <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H7307" data-style="w">wind</span> driveth <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H5086" data-style="w">away</span>.</span><br class="topos-l"><span class="topos-l" data-style="q1"><span class="topos-verse" data-osis-id="PSA 1:5" data-n="5"></span> Therefore the <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H7563" data-style="w">ungodly</span> shall not <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H6965" data-style="w">stand</span> in the <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H4941" data-style="w">judgment</span>, nor <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H2400" data-style="w">sinners</span> in the <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H5712" data-style="w">congregation</span> of the <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H6662" data-style="w">righteous</span>.</span><br class="topos-l"><span class="topos-l" data-style="q1"><span class="topos-verse" data-osis-id="PSA 1:6" data-n="6"></span> For the <span class="topos-divine-name" data-style="nd"><span class="topos-w" data-strong="H3068" data-style="w">LORD</span></span> <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H3045" data-style="w">knoweth</span> the <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H1870" data-style="w">way</span> of the <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H6662" data-style="w">righteous</span>: but the <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H1870" data-style="w">way</span> of the <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H7563" data-style="w">ungodly</span> shall <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H6" data-style="w">perish</span>.</span><br class="topos-l"><span class="topos-chapter" data-osis-id="PSA 2" data-n="2"></span><span class="topos-l" data-style="q1"><span class="topos-verse" data-osis-id="PSA 2:1" data-n="1"></span> Why do the <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H1471" data-style="w">heathen</span> <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H7283" data-style="w">rage</span>, and the <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H3816" data-style="w">people</span> <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H1897" data-style="w">imagine</span> a vain <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H7385" data-style="w">thing</span>?<span class="topos-note topos-footnote" data-note-type="footnote" data-n="+" data-style="f"><span class="topos-char" data-style="fr">2.1 </span><span class="topos-char" data-style="ft">rage: or, tumultuously assemble</span></span><span class="topos-note topos-footnote" data-note-type="footnote" data-n="+" data-style="f"><span class="topos-char" data-style="fr">2.1 </span><span class="topos-char" data-style="ft">imagine: Heb. meditate</span></span></span><br class="topos-l"><span class="topos-l" data-style="q1"><span class="topos-verse" data-osis-id="PSA 2:2" data-n="2"></span> The <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H4428" data-style="w">kings</span> of the <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H776" data-style="w">earth</span> <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H3320" data-style="w">set</span> themselves, and the <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H7336" data-style="w">rulers</span> take <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H3245" data-style="w">counsel</span> <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H3162" data-style="w">together</span>, against the <span class="topos-divine-name" data-style="nd"><span class="topos-w" data-strong="H3068" data-style="w">LORD</span></span>, and against his <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H4899" data-style="w">anointed</span>, <span class="topos-added" data-style="add">saying</span>,</span><br class="topos-l"><span class="topos-l" data-style="q1"><span class="topos-verse" data-osis-id="PSA 2:3" data-n="3"></span> Let us <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H5423" data-style="w">break</span> their <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H4147" data-style="w">bands</span> <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H5423" data-style="w">asunder</span>, and cast <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H7993" data-style="w">away</span> their <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H5688" data-style="w">cords</span> from us.</span><br class="topos-l"><span class="topos-l" data-style="q1"><span class="topos-verse" data-osis-id="PSA 2:4" data-n="4"></span> He that <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H3427" data-style="w">sitteth</span> in the <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H8064" data-style="w">heavens</span> shall <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H7832" data-style="w">laugh</span>: the <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H136" data-style="w">Lord</span> shall have them in <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H3932" data-style="w">derision</span>.</span><br class="topos-l"><span class="topos-l" data-style="q1"><span class="topos-verse" data-osis-id="PSA 2:5" data-n="5"></span> Then shall he <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H1696" data-style="w">speak</span> unto them in his <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H639" data-style="w">wrath</span>, and <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H926" data-style="w">vex</span> them in his sore <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H2740" data-style="w">displeasure</span>.<span class="topos-note topos-footnote" data-note-type="footnote" data-n="+" data-style="f"><span class="topos-char" data-style="fr">2.5 </span><span class="topos-char" data-style="ft">vex: or, trouble</span></span></span><br class="topos-l"><span class="topos-l" data-style="q1"><span class="topos-verse" data-osis-id="PSA 2:6" data-n="6"></span> Yet have I <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H5258" data-style="w">set</span> my <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H4428" data-style="w">king</span> upon my <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H6944" data-style="w">holy</span> <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H2022" data-style="w">hill</span> of <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H6726" data-style="w">Zion</span>.<span class="topos-note topos-footnote" data-note-type="footnote" data-n="+" data-style="f"><span class="topos-char" data-style="fr">2.6 </span><span class="topos-char" data-style="ft">set: Heb. anointed</span></span><span class="topos-note topos-footnote" data-note-type="footnote" data-n="+" data-style="f"><span class="topos-char" data-style="fr">2.6 </span><span class="topos-char" data-style="ft">upon…: Heb. upon Zion, the hill of my holiness</span></span></span><br class="topos-l"><br class="topos-lb" data-style="b"><span class="topos-l" data-style="q1"><span class="topos-verse" data-osis-id="PSA 2:7" data-n="7"></span> I will <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H5608" data-style="w">declare</span> the <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H2706" data-style="w">decree</span>: the <span class="topos-divine-name" data-style="nd"><span class="topos-w" data-strong="H3068" data-style="w">LORD</span></span> hath <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H559" data-style="w">said</span> unto me, Thou <span class="topos-added" data-style="add">art</span> my <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H1121" data-style="w">Son</span>; this <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H3117" data-style="w">day</span> have I <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H3205" data-style="w">begotten</span> thee.<span class="topos-note topos-footnote" data-note-type="footnote" data-n="+" data-style="f"><span class="topos-char" data-style="fr">2.7 </span><span class="topos-char" data-style="ft">the decree: or, for a decree</span></span></span><br class="topos-l"><span class="topos-l" data-style="q1"><span class="topos-verse" data-osis-id="PSA 2:8" data-n="8"></span> <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H7592" data-style="w">Ask</span> of me, and I shall <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H5414" data-style="w">give</span> <span class="topos-added" data-style="add">thee</span> the <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H1471" data-style="w">heathen</span> <span class="topos-added" data-style="add">for</span> thine <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H5159" data-style="w">inheritance</span>, and the uttermost <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H657" data-style="w">parts</span> of the <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H776" data-style="w">earth</span> <span class="topos-added" data-style="add">for</span> thy <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H272" data-style="w">possession</span>.</span><br class="topos-l"><span class="topos-l" data-style="q1"><span class="topos-verse" data-osis-id="PSA 2:9" data-n="9"></span> Thou shalt <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H7489" data-style="w">break</span> them with a <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H7626" data-style="w">rod</span> of <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H1270" data-style="w">iron</span>; thou shalt dash them in <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H5310" data-style="w">pieces</span> like a <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H3335" data-style="w">potter’s</span> <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H3627" data-style="w">vessel</span>.</span><br class="topos-l"><br class="topos-lb" data-style="b"><span class="topos-l" data-style="q1"><span class="topos-verse" data-osis-id="PSA 2:10" data-n="10"></span> Be <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H7919" data-style="w">wise</span> now therefore, O ye <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H4428" data-style="w">kings</span>: be <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H3256" data-style="w">instructed</span>, ye <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H8199" data-style="w">judges</span> of the <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H776" data-style="w">earth</span>.</span><br class="topos-l"><span class="topos-l" data-style="q1"><span class="topos-verse" data-osis-id="PSA 2:11" data-n="11"></span> <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H5647" data-style="w">Serve</span> the <span class="topos-divine-name" data-style="nd"><span class="topos-w" data-strong="H3068" data-style="w">LORD</span></span> with <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H3374" data-style="w">fear</span>, and <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H1523" data-style="w">rejoice</span> with <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H7461" data-style="w">trembling</span>.</span><br class="topos-l"><span class="topos-l" data-style="q1"><span class="topos-verse" data-osis-id="PSA 2:12" data-n="12"></span> <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H5401" data-style="w">Kiss</span> the <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H1248" data-style="w">Son</span>, lest he be <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H599" data-style="w">angry</span>, and ye <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H6" data-style="w">perish</span> <span class="topos-added" data-style="add">from</span> the <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H1870" data-style="w">way</span>, when his <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H639" data-style="w">wrath</span> is <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H1197" data-style="w">kindled</span> but a <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H4592" data-style="w">little</span>. <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H835" data-style="w">Blessed</span> <span class="topos-added" data-style="add">are</span> all they that put their <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H2620" data-style="w">trust</span> in him.</span><br class="topos-l"><span class="topos-chapter" data-osis-id="PSA 3" data-n="3"></span><div class="topos-title topos-d" data-title-type="d" data-style="d">A <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H4210" data-style="w">Psalm</span> of <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H1732" data-style="w">David</span>, when he <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H1272" data-style="w">fled</span> <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H6440" data-style="w">from</span> <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H53" data-style="w">Absalom</span> his <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H1121" data-style="w">son</span>.</div><span class="topos-l" data-style="q1"><span class="topos-verse" data-osis-id="PSA 3:1" data-n="1"></span> <span class="topos-divine-name" data-style="nd"><span class="topos-w" data-strong="H3068" data-style="w">LORD</span></span>, how are they <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H7231" data-style="w">increased</span> that <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H6862" data-style="w">trouble</span> me! <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H7227" data-style="w">many</span> <span class="topos-added" data-style="add">are</span> they that rise <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H6965" data-style="w">up</span> against me.</span><br class="topos-l"><span class="topos-l" data-style="q1"><span class="topos-verse" data-osis-id="PSA 3:2" data-n="2"></span> <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H7227" data-style="w">Many</span> <span class="topos-added" data-style="add">there be</span> which <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H559" data-style="w">say</span> of my <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H5315" data-style="w">soul</span>, <span class="topos-added" data-style="add">There is</span> no <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H3444" data-style="w">help</span> for him in <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H430" data-style="w">God</span>. <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H5542" data-style="w">Selah</span>.</span><br class="topos-l"><span class="topos-l" data-style="q1"><span class="topos-verse" data-osis-id="PSA 3:3" data-n="3"></span> But thou, O <span class="topos-divine-name" data-style="nd"><span class="topos-w" data-strong="H3068" data-style="w">LORD</span></span>, <span class="topos-added" data-style="add">art</span> a <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H4043" data-style="w">shield</span> for me; my <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H3519" data-style="w">glory</span>, and the lifter <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H7311" data-style="w">up</span> of mine <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H7218" data-style="w">head</span>.<span class="topos-note topos-footnote" data-note-type="footnote" data-n="+" data-style="f"><span class="topos-char" data-style="fr">3.3 </span><span class="topos-char" data-style="ft">for: or, about</span></span></span><br class="topos-l"><br class="topos-lb" data-style="b"><span class="topos-l" data-style="q1"><span class="topos-verse" data-osis-id="PSA 3:4" data-n="4"></span> I <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H7121" data-style="w">cried</span> unto the <span class="topos-divine-name" data-style="nd"><span class="topos-w" data-strong="H3068" data-style="w">LORD</span></span> with my <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H6963" data-style="w">voice</span>, and he <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H6030" data-style="w">heard</span> me out of his <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H6944" data-style="w">holy</span> <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H2022" data-style="w">hill</span>. <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H5542" data-style="w">Selah</span>.</span><br class="topos-l"><span class="topos-l" data-style="q1"><span class="topos-verse" data-osis-id="PSA 3:5" data-n="5"></span> I laid me <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H7901" data-style="w">down</span> and <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H3462" data-style="w">slept</span>; I <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H6974" data-style="w">awaked</span>; for the <span class="topos-divine-name" data-style="nd"><span class="topos-w" data-strong="H3068" data-style="w">LORD</span></span> <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H5564" data-style="w">sustained</span> me.</span><br class="topos-l"><span class="topos-l" data-style="q1"><span class="topos-verse" data-osis-id="PSA 3:6" data-n="6"></span> I will not be <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H3372" data-style="w">afraid</span> of ten <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H7233" data-style="w">thousands</span> of <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H5971" data-style="w">people</span>, that have <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H7896" data-style="w">set</span> <span class="topos-added" data-style="add">themselves</span> against me round <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H5439" data-style="w">about</span>.</span><br class="topos-l"><span class="topos-l" data-style="q1"><span class="topos-verse" data-osis-id="PSA 3:7" data-n="7"></span> <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H6965" data-style="w">Arise</span>, O <span class="topos-divine-name" data-style="nd"><span class="topos-w" data-strong="H3068" data-style="w">LORD</span></span>; <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H3467" data-style="w">save</span> me, O my <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H430" data-style="w">God</span>: for thou hast <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H5221" data-style="w">smitten</span> all mine <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H341" data-style="w">enemies</span> <span class="topos-added" data-style="add">upon</span> the cheek <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H3895" data-style="w">bone</span>; thou hast <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H7665" data-style="w">broken</span> the <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H8127" data-style="w">teeth</span> of the <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H7563" data-style="w">ungodly</span>.</span><br class="topos-l"><span class="topos-l" data-style="q1"><span class="topos-verse" data-osis-id="PSA 3:8" data-n="8"></span> <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H3444" data-style="w">Salvation</span> <span class="topos-added" data-style="add">belongeth</span> unto the <span class="topos-divine-name" data-style="nd"><span class="topos-w" data-strong="H3068" data-style="w">LORD</span></span>: thy <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H1293" data-style="w">blessing</span> <span class="topos-added" data-style="add">is</span> upon thy <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H5971" data-style="w">people</span>. <span class="topos-w" data-strong="H5542" data-style="w">Selah</span>.</span><br class="topos-l">
#### html-bare ####
PsalmsPsalmsThe Book of PsalmsPsalmsPsa<div class="title mt1" data-title-type="mt1" data-style="mt1">The Book of Psalms</div><span class="chapter" data-osis-id="PSA 1" data-n="1"></span><span class="l" data-style="q1"><span class="verse" data-osis-id="PSA 1:1" data-n="1"></span> <span class="w" data-strong="H835" data-style="w">Blessed</span> <span class="added" data-style="add">is</span> the <span class="w" data-strong="H376" data-style="w">man</span> that <span class="w" data-strong="H1980" data-style="w">walketh</span> not in the <span class="w" data-strong="H6098" data-style="w">counsel</span> of the <span class="w" data-strong="H7563" data-style="w">ungodly</span>, nor <span class="w" data-strong="H5975" data-style="w">standeth</span> in the <span class="w" data-strong="H1870" data-style="w">way</span> of <span class="w" data-strong="H2400" data-style="w">sinners</span>, nor <span class="w" data-strong="H3427" data-style="w">sitteth</span> in the <span class="w" data-strong="H4186" data-style="w">seat</span> of the <span class="w" data-strong="H3887" data-style="w">scornful</span>.<span class="note footnote" data-note-type="footnote" data-n="+" data-style="f"><span class="char" data-style="fr">1.1 </span><span class="char" data-style="ft">ungodly: or, wicked</span></span></span><br class="l"><span class="l" data-style="q1"><span class="verse" data-osis-id="PSA 1:2" data-n="2"></span> But his <span class="w" data-strong="H2656" data-style="w">delight</span> <span class="added" data-style="add">is</span> in the <span class="w" data-strong="H8451" data-style="w">law</span> of the <span class="divine-name" data-style="nd"><span class="w" data-strong="H3068" data-style="w">LORD</span></span>; and in his <span class="w" data-strong="H8451" data-style="w">law</span> doth he <span class="w" data-strong="H1897" data-style="w">meditate</span> <span class="w" data-strong="H3119" data-style="w">day</span> and <span class="w" data-strong="H3915" data-style="w">night</span>.</span><br class="l"><span class="l" data-style="q1"><span class="verse" data-osis-id="PSA 1:3" data-n="3"></span> And he shall be like a <span class="w" data-strong="H6086" data-style="w">tree</span> <span class="w" data-strong="H8362" data-style="w">planted</span> by the <span class="w" data-strong="H6388" data-style="w">rivers</span> of <span class="w" data-strong="H4325" data-style="w">water</span>, that bringeth <span class="w" data-strong="H5414" data-style="w">forth</span> his <span class="w" data-strong="H6529" data-style="w">fruit</span> in his <span class="w" data-strong="H6256" data-style="w">season</span>; his <span class="w" data-strong="H5929" data-style="w">leaf</span> also shall not <span class="w" data-strong="H5034" data-style="w">wither</span>; and whatsoever he <span class="w" data-strong="H6213" data-style="w">doeth</span> shall <span class="w" data-strong="H6743" data-style="w">prosper</span>.<span class="note footnote" data-note-type="footnote" data-n="+" data-style="f"><span class="char" data-style="fr">1.3 </span><span class="char" data-style="ft">wither: Heb. fade</span></span></span><br class="l"><br class="lb" data-style="b"><span class="l" data-style="q1"><span class="verse" data-osis-id="PSA 1:4" data-n="4"></span> The <span class="w" data-strong="H7563" data-style="w">ungodly</span> <span class="added" data-style="add">are</span> not so: but <span class="added" data-style="add">are</span> like the <span class="w" data-strong="H4671" data-style="w">chaff</span> which the <span class="w" data-strong="H7307" data-style="w">wind</span> driveth <span class="w" data-strong="H5086" data-style="w">away</span>.</span><br class="l"><span class="l" data-style="q1"><span class="verse" data-osis-id="PSA 1:5" data-n="5"></span> Therefore the <span class="w" data-strong="H7563" data-style="w">ungodly</span> shall not <span class="w" data-strong="H6965" data-style="w">stand</span> in the <span class="w" data-strong="H4941" data-style="w">judgment</span>, nor <span class="w" data-strong="H2400" data-style="w">sinners</span> in the <span class="w" data-strong="H5712" data-style="w">congregation</span> of the <span class="w" data-strong="H6662" data-style="w">righteous</span>.</span><br class="l"><span class="l" data-style="q1"><span class="verse" data-osis-id="PSA 1:6" data-n="6"></span> For the <span class="divine-name" data-style="nd"><span class="w" data-strong="H3068" data-style="w">LORD</span></span> <span class="w" data-strong="H3045" data-style="w">knoweth</span> the <span class="w" data-strong="H1870" data-style="w">way</span> of the <span class="w" data-strong="H6662" data-style="w">righteous</span>: but the <span class="w" data-strong="H1870" data-style="w">way</span> of the <span class="w" data-strong="H7563" data-style="w">ungodly</span> shall <span class="w" data-strong="H6" data-style="w">perish</span>.</span><br class="l"><span class="chapter" data-osis-id="PSA 2" data-n="2"></span><span class="l" data-style="q1"><span class="verse" data-osis-id="PSA 2:1" data-n="1"></span> Why do the <span class="w" data-strong="H1471" data-style="w">heathen</span> <span class="w" data-strong="H7283" data-style="w">rage</span>, and the <span class="w" data-strong="H3816" data-style="w">people</span> <span class="w" data-strong="H1897" data-style="w">imagine</span> a vain <span class="w" data-strong="H7385" data-style="w">thing</span>?<span class="note footnote" data-note-type="footnote" data-n="+" data-style="f"><span class="char" data-style="fr">2.1 </span><span class="char" data-style="ft">rage: or, tumultuously assemble</span></span><span class="note footnote" data-note-type="footnote" data-n="+" data-style="f"><span class="char" data-style="fr">2.1 </span><span class="char" data-style="ft">imagine: Heb. meditate</span></span></span><br class="l"><span class="l" data-style="q1"><span class="verse" data-osis-id="PSA 2:2" data-n="2"></span> The <span class="w" data-strong="H4428" data-style="w">kings</span> of the <span class="w" data-strong="H776" data-style="w">earth</span> <span class="w" data-strong="H3320" data-style="w">set</span> themselves, and the <span class="w" data-strong="H7336" data-style="w">rulers</span> take <span class="w" data-strong="H3245" data-style="w">counsel</span> <span class="w" data-strong="H3162" data-style="w">together</span>, against the <span class="divine-name" data-style="nd"><span class="w" data-strong="H3068" data-style="w">LORD</span></span>, and against his <span class="w" data-strong="H4899" data-style="w">anointed</span>, <span class="added" data-style="add">saying</span>,</span><br class="l"><span class="l" data-style="q1"><span class="verse" data-osis-id="PSA 2:3" data-n="3"></span> Let us <span class="w" data-strong="H5423" data-style="w">break</span> their <span class="w" data-strong="H4147" data-style="w">bands</span> <span class="w" data-strong="H5423" data-style="w">asunder</span>, and cast <span class="w" data-strong="H7993" data-style="w">away</span> their <span class="w" data-strong="H5688" data-style="w">cords</span> from us.</span><br class="l"><span class="l" data-style="q1"><span class="verse" data-osis-id="PSA 2:4" data-n="4"></span> He that <span class="w" data-strong="H3427" data-style="w">sitteth</span> in the <span class="w" data-strong="H8064" data-style="w">heavens</span> shall <span class="w" data-strong="H7832" data-style="w">laugh</span>: the <span class="w" data-strong="H136" data-style="w">Lord</span> shall have them in <span class="w" data-strong="H3932" data-style="w">derision</span>.</span><br class="l"><span class="l" data-style="q1"><span class="verse" data-osis-id="PSA 2:5" data-n="5"></span> Then shall he <span class="w" data-strong="H1696" data-style="w">speak</span> unto them in his <span class="w" data-strong="H639" data-style="w">wrath</span>, and <span class="w" data-strong="H926" data-style="w">vex</span> them in his sore <span class="w" data-strong="H2740" data-style="w">displeasure</span>.<span class="note footnote" data-note-type="footnote" data-n="+" data-style="f"><span class="char" data-style="fr">2.5 </span><span class="char" data-style="ft">vex: or, trouble</span></span></span><br class="l"><span class="l" data-style="q1"><span class="verse" data-osis-id="PSA 2:6" data-n="6"></span> Yet have I <span class="w" data-strong="H5258" data-style="w">set</span> my <span class="w" data-strong="H4428" data-style="w">king</span> upon my <span class="w" data-strong="H6944" data-style="w">holy</span> <span class="w" data-strong="H2022" data-style="w">hill</span> of <span class="w" data-strong="H6726" data-style="w">Zion</span>.<span class="note footnote" data-note-type="footnote" data-n="+" data-style="f"><span class="char" data-style="fr">2.6 </span><span class="char" data-style="ft">set: Heb. anointed</span></span><span class="note footnote" data-note-type="footnote" data-n="+" data-style="f"><span class="char" data-style="fr">2.6 </span><span class="char" data-style="ft">upon…: Heb. upon Zion, the hill of my holiness</span></span></span><br class="l"><br class="lb" data-style="b"><span class="l" data-style="q1"><span class="verse" data-osis-id="PSA 2:7" data-n="7"></span> I will <span class="w" data-strong="H5608" data-style="w">declare</span> the <span class="w" data-strong="H2706" data-style="w">decree</span>: the <span class="divine-name" data-style="nd"><span class="w" data-strong="H3068" data-style="w">LORD</span></span> hath <span class="w" data-strong="H559" data-style="w">said</span> unto me, Thou <span class="added" data-style="add">art</span> my <span class="w" data-strong="H1121" data-style="w">Son</span>; this <span class="w" data-strong="H3117" data-style="w">day</span> have I <span class="w" data-strong="H3205" data-style="w">begotten</span> thee.<span class="note footnote" data-note-type="footnote" data-n="+" data-style="f"><span class="char" data-style="fr">2.7 </span><span class="char" data-style="ft">the decree: or, for a decree</span></span></span><br class="l"><span class="l" data-style="q1"><span class="verse" data-osis-id="PSA 2:8" data-n="8"></span> <span class="w" data-strong="H7592" data-style="w">Ask</span> of me, and I shall <span class="w" data-strong="H5414" data-style="w">give</span> <span class="added" data-style="add">thee</span> the <span class="w" data-strong="H1471" data-style="w">heathen</span> <span class="added" data-style="add">for</span> thine <span class="w" data-strong="H5159" data-style="w">inheritance</span>, and the uttermost <span class="w" data-strong="H657" data-style="w">parts</span> of the <span class="w" data-strong="H776" data-style="w">earth</span> <span class="added" data-style="add">for</span> thy <span class="w" data-strong="H272" data-style="w">possession</span>.</span><br class="l"><span class="l" data-style="q1"><span class="verse" data-osis-id="PSA 2:9" data-n="9"></span> Thou shalt <span class="w" data-strong="H7489" data-style="w">break</span> them with a <span class="w" data-strong="H7626" data-style="w">rod</span> of <span class="w" data-strong="H1270" data-style="w">iron</span>; thou shalt dash them in <span class="w" data-strong="H5310" data-style="w">pieces</span> like a <span class="w" data-strong="H3335" data-style="w">potter’s</span> <span class="w" data-strong="H3627" data-style="w">vessel</span>.</span><br class="l"><br class="lb" data-style="b"><span class="l" data-style="q1"><span class="verse" data-osis-id="PSA 2:10" data-n="10"></span> Be <span class="w" data-strong="H7919" data-style="w">wise</span> now therefore, O ye <span class="w" data-strong="H4428" data-style="w">kings</span>: be <span class="w" data-strong="H3256" data-style="w">instructed</span>, ye <span class="w" data-strong="H8199" data-style="w">judges</span> of the <span class="w" data-strong="H776" data-style="w">earth</span>.</span><br class="l"><span class="l" data-style="q1"><span class="verse" data-osis-id="PSA 2:11" data-n="11"></span> <span class="w" data-strong="H5647" data-style="w">Serve</span> the <span class="divine-name" data-style="nd"><span class="w" data-strong="H3068" data-style="w">LORD</span></span> with <span class="w" data-strong="H3374" data-style="w">fear</span>, and <span class="w" data-strong="H1523" data-style="w">rejoice</span> with <span class="w" data-strong="H7461" data-style="w">trembling</span>.</span><br class="l"><span class="l" data-style="q1"><span class="verse" data-osis-id="PSA 2:12" data-n="12"></span> <span class="w" data-strong="H5401" data-style="w">Kiss</span> the <span class="w" data-strong="H1248" data-style="w">Son</span>, lest he be <span class="w" data-strong="H599" data-style="w">angry</span>, and ye <span class="w" data-strong="H6" data-style="w">perish</span> <span class="added" data-style="add">from</span> the <span class="w" data-strong="H1870" data-style="w">way</span>, when his <span class="w" data-strong="H639" data-style="w">wrath</span> is <span class="w" data-strong="H1197" data-style="w">kindled</span> but a <span class="w" data-strong="H4592" data-style="w">little</span>. <span class="w" data-strong="H835" data-style="w">Blessed</span> <span class="added" data-style="add">are</span> all they that put their <span class="w" data-strong="H2620" data-style="w">trust</span> in him.</span><br class="l"><span class="chapter" data-osis-id="PSA 3" data-n="3"></span><div class="title d" data-title-type="d" data-style="d">A <span class="w" data-strong="H4210" data-style="w">Psalm</span> of <span class="w" data-strong="H1732" data-style="w">David</span>, when he <span class="w" data-strong="H1272" data-style="w">fled</span> <span class="w" data-strong="H6440" data-style="w">from</span> <span class="w" data-strong="H53" data-style="w">Absalom</span> his <span class="w" data-strong="H1121" data-style="w">son</span>.</div><span class="l" data-style="q1"><span class="verse" data-osis-id="PSA 3:1" data-n="1"></span> <span class="divine-name" data-style="nd"><span class="w" data-strong="H3068" data-style="w">LORD</span></span>, how are they <span class="w" data-strong="H7231" data-style="w">increased</span> that <span class="w" data-strong="H6862" data-style="w">trouble</span> me! <span class="w" data-strong="H7227" data-style="w">many</span> <span class="added" data-style="add">are</span> they that rise <span class="w" data-strong="H6965" data-style="w">up</span> against me.</span><br class="l"><span class="l" data-style="q1"><span class="verse" data-osis-id="PSA 3:2" data-n="2"></span> <span class="w" data-strong="H7227" data-style="w">Many</span> <span class="added" data-style="add">there be</span> which <span class="w" data-strong="H559" data-style="w">say</span> of my <span class="w" data-strong="H5315" data-style="w">soul</span>, <span class="added" data-style="add">There is</span> no <span class="w" data-strong="H3444" data-style="w">help</span> for him in <span class="w" data-strong="H430" data-style="w">God</span>. <span class="w" data-strong="H5542" data-style="w">Selah</span>.</span><br class="l"><span class="l" data-style="q1"><span class="verse" data-osis-id="PSA 3:3" data-n="3"></span> But thou, O <span class="divine-name" data-style="nd"><span class="w" data-strong="H3068" data-style="w">LORD</span></span>, <span class="added" data-style="add">art</span> a <span class="w" data-strong="H4043" data-style="w">shield</span> for me; my <span class="w" data-strong="H3519" data-style="w">glory</span>, and the lifter <span class="w" data-strong="H7311" data-style="w">up</span> of mine <span class="w" data-strong="H7218" data-style="w">head</span>.<span class="note footnote" data-note-type="footnote" data-n="+" data-style="f"><span class="char" data-style="fr">3.3 </span><span class="char" data-style="ft">for: or, about</span></span></span><br class="l"><br class="lb" data-style="b"><span class="l" data-style="q1"><span class="verse" data-osis-id="PSA 3:4" data-n="4"></span> I <span class="w" data-strong="H7121" data-style="w">cried</span> unto the <span class="divine-name" data-style="nd"><span class="w" data-strong="H3068" data-style="w">LORD</span></span> with my <span class="w" data-strong="H6963" data-style="w">voice</span>, and he <span class="w" data-strong="H6030" data-style="w">heard</span> me out of his <span class="w" data-strong="H6944" data-style="w">holy</span> <span class="w" data-strong="H2022" data-style="w">hill</span>. <span class="w" data-strong="H5542" data-style="w">Selah</span>.</span><br class="l"><span class="l" data-style="q1"><span class="verse" data-osis-id="PSA 3:5" data-n="5"></span> I laid me <span class="w" data-strong="H7901" data-style="w">down</span> and <span class="w" data-strong="H3462" data-style="w">slept</span>; I <span class="w" data-strong="H6974" data-style="w">awaked</span>; for the <span class="divine-name" data-style="nd"><span class="w" data-strong="H3068" data-style="w">LORD</span></span> <span class="w" data-strong="H5564" data-style="w">sustained</span> me.</span><br class="l"><span class="l" data-style="q1"><span class="verse" data-osis-id="PSA 3:6" data-n="6"></span> I will not be <span class="w" data-strong="H3372" data-style="w">afraid</span> of ten <span class="w" data-strong="H7233" data-style="w">thousands</span> of <span class="w" data-strong="H5971" data-style="w">people</span>, that have <span class="w" data-strong="H7896" data-style="w">set</span> <span class="added" data-style="add">themselves</span> against me round <span class="w" data-strong="H5439" data-style="w">about</span>.</span><br class="l"><span class="l" data-style="q1"><span class="verse" data-osis-id="PSA 3:7" data-n="7"></span> <span class="w" data-strong="H6965" data-style="w">Arise</span>, O <span class="divine-name" data-style="nd"><span class="w" data-strong="H3068" data-style="w">LORD</span></span>; <span class="w" data-strong="H3467" data-style="w">save</span> me, O my <span class="w" data-strong="H430" data-style="w">God</span>: for thou hast <span class="w" data-strong="H5221" data-style="w">smitten</span> all mine <span class="w" data-strong="H341" data-style="w">enemies</span> <span class="added" data-style="add">upon</span> the cheek <span class="w" data-strong="H3895" data-style="w">bone</span>; thou hast <span class="w" data-strong="H7665" data-style="w">broken</span> the <span class="w" data-strong="H8127" data-style="w">teeth</span> of the <span class="w" data-strong="H7563" data-style="w">ungodly</span>.</span><br class="l"><span class="l" data-style="q1"><span class="verse" data-osis-id="PSA 3:8" data-n="8"></span> <span class="w" data-strong="H3444" data-style="w">Salvation</span> <span class="added" data-style="add">belongeth</span> unto the <span class="divine-name" data-style="nd"><span class="w" data-strong="H3068" data-style="w">LORD</span></span>: thy <span class="w" data-strong="H1293" data-style="w">blessing</span> <span class="added" data-style="add">is</span> upon thy <span class="w" data-strong="H5971" data-style="w">people</span>. <span class="w" data-strong="H5542" data-style="w">Selah</span>.</span><br class="l">
#### verses ####
1:1-1 marker=/0/7/0 start=/0/7 end=/0/8/0 "Blessed is the man that walketh not in the counsel of the ungodly, nor standeth in the way of sinners, nor sitteth in the seat of the scornful. [1.1 ungodly: or, wicked]"
1:2-2 marker=/0/8/1 start=/0/8/1 end=/0/9/0 "But his delight is in the law of the LORD; and in his law doth he meditate day and night."
1:3-3 marker=/0/9/1 start=/0/9/1 end=/0/11/0 "And he shall be like a tree planted by the rivers of water, that bringeth forth his fruit in his season; his leaf also shall not wither; and whatsoever he doeth shall prosper. [1.3 wither: Heb. fade]"
1:4-4 marker=/0/11/1 start=/0/11/1 end=/0/12/0 "The ungodly are not so: but are like the chaff which the wind driveth away."
1:5-5 marker=/0/12/1 start=/0/12/1 end=/0/13/0 "Therefore the ungodly shall not stand in the judgment, nor sinners in the congregation of the righteous."
1:6-6 marker=/0/13/1 start=/0/13/1 end=/0/14 "For the LORD knoweth the way of the righteous: but the way of the ungodly shall perish."
2:1-1 marker=/0/17/0 start=/0/17 end=/0/18/0 "Why do the heathen rage, and the people imagine a vain thing? [2.1 rage: or, tumultuously assemble] [2.1 imagine: Heb. meditate]"
2:2-2 marker=/0/18/1 start=/0/18/1 end=/0/19/0 "The kings of the earth set themselves, and the rulers take counsel together, against the LORD, and against his anointed, saying,"
2:3-3 marker=/0/19/1 start=/0/19/1 end=/0/20/0 "Let us break their bands asunder, and cast away their cords from us."
2:4-4 marker=/0/20/1 start=/0/20/1 end=/0/21/0 "He that sitteth in the heavens shall laugh: the Lord shall have them in derision."
2:5-5 marker=/0/21/1 start=/0/21/1 end=/0/22/0 "Then shall he speak unto them in his wrath, and vex them in his sore displeasure. [2.5 vex: or, trouble]"
2:6-6 marker=/0/22/1 start=/0/22/1 end=/0/24/0 "Yet have I set my king upon my holy hill of Zion. [2.6 set: Heb. anointed] [2.6 upon…: Heb. upon Zion, the hill of my holiness]"
2:7-7 marker=/0/24/1 start=/0/24/1 end=/0/25/0 "I will declare the decree: the LORD hath said unto me, Thou art my Son; this day have I begotten thee. [2.7 the decree: or, for a decree]"
2:8-8 marker=/0/25/1 start=/0/25/1 end=/0/26/0 "Ask of me, and I shall give thee the heathen for thine inheritance, and the uttermost parts of the earth for thy possession."
2:9-9 marker=/0/26/1 start=/0/26/1 end=/0/28/0 "Thou shalt break them with a rod of iron; thou shalt dash them in pieces like a potter’s vessel."
2:10-10 marker=/0/28/1 start=/0/28/1 end=/0/29/0 "Be wise now therefore, O ye kings: be instructed, ye judges of the earth."
2:11-11 marker=/0/29/1 start=/0/29/1 end=/0/30/0 "Serve the LORD with fear, and rejoice with trembling."
2:12-12 marker=/0/30/1 start=/0/30/1 end=/0/31 "Kiss the Son, lest he be angry, and ye perish from the way, when his wrath is kindled but a little. Blessed are all they that put their trust in him."
3:1-1 marker=/0/35/0 start=/0/34 end=/0/36/0 "A Psalm of David, when he fled from Absalom his son.\nLORD, how are they increased that trouble me! many are they that rise up against me."
3:2-2 marker=/0/36/1 start=/0/36/1 end=/0/37/0 "Many there be which say of my soul, There is no help for him in God. Selah."
3:3-3 marker=/0/37/1 start=/0/37/1 end=/0/39/0 "But thou, O LORD, art a shield for me; my glory, and the lifter up of mine head. [3.3 for: or, about]"
3:4-4 marker=/0/39/1 start=/0/39/1 end=/0/40/0 "I cried unto the LORD with my voice, and he heard me out of his holy hill. Selah."
3:5-5 marker=/0/40/1 start=/0/40/1 end=/0/41/0 "I laid me down and slept; I awaked; for the LORD sustained me."
3:6-6 marker=/0/41/1 start=/0/41/1 end=/0/42/0 "I will not be afraid of ten thousands of people, that have set themselves against me round about."
3:7-7 marker=/0/42/1 start=/0/42/1 end=/0/43/0 "Arise, O LORD; save me, O my God: for thou hast smitten all mine enemies upon the cheek bone; thou hast broken the teeth of the ungodly."
3:8-8 marker=/0/43/1 start=/0/43/1 end=/0/44 "Salvation belongeth unto the LORD: thy blessing is upon thy people. Selah."
chapter_verses: [6, 12, 8]

#### usx-chapter-verses ####
[6, 12, 8]

#### refs ####

